    notification, the accurate one.
  - [1mCompleting or unwatching a task stops future reminders but doesn't retract delivered ones.[0m They're history, not live
    state.

  [1mCadence.[0m A 60-second tick, plus a run on task change and on [38;5;153mvisibilitychange[39m. Everything is computed from absolute
  timestamps, never from counting elapsed intervals — so a throttled background tab, a laptop sleeping through a
  deadline, or a clock change all resolve into an ordinary catch-up tick rather than drift or a missed reminder.

  [1mWhere a notification appears.[0m Always the tray. Additionally: a toast if the tab is visible, or an OS notification if
  it's hidden and permission was granted. Never both toast and OS popup for the same event — that's the same
  interruption twice.

  [1mToasts.[0m Max 3 stacked, 5s auto-dismiss (10s when carrying an undo action), hover pauses the timer. Undo exists for
  delete only; that's the one action where a misclick actually costs something. If you want less surface, undo is the
  first thing I'd cut.

  [1mAccessibility.[0m Toasts announced via [38;5;153maria-live="polite"[39m, tray badge carries an accessible label with the unread count,
  tray is keyboard-reachable and closes on Escape, and nothing steals focus — a notification interrupting someone
  mid-sentence in a task title is worse than the notification is useful.

  [1mBounding growth.[0m The stored notification list is capped at 100, trimming oldest-read-first, so localStorage can't grow
  without limit.
